==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἔκζεμα}}, from {{m|grc|ἐκ||out of, forth from}} + {{m|grc|ζέμα||that which is boiled, decoction}}, from {{m|grc|ζέω||to boil, to seethe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈɛɡzɪmə/|/ˈɛksɪmə/|/ˈɛksmə/|lang=en}}
* {{a|Canada|US}} {{IPA|/ɪɡˈzimə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|eczemata|eczemas}}

# An acute or chronic [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by redness, itching, and the outbreak of oozing [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become encrusted and scaly. It is noncontagious.

